{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534473-other-cultures-sphere-systems","id":1534473,"title":"other cultures sphere systems","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-04-19T18:24:35-07:00","id":1534473,"title":"other cultures sphere systems","content":"how do other cultures classify magic? the kopa loei have a well detailed, non sphere system, but others havent been detailed. what would they be like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27683-bernese","name":"Bernese","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-19T19:41:04-07:00","id":1534476,"title":"","content":"As a general rule I assume you'd need to understand a culture's categories to answer that question. A West African &quot;Sphere&quot; system would likely involve either four or sixteen because those numbers symbolize totality and completion. Thus the importance of the Goddess Oshun being symbolized by five and seventeen. Oshun is the unknowns that secretly power and complete the world. <br /> <br /> Five tends to be an important number in East Asian countries. Eight is vastly important in Taoist lands especially China and Korea. <br /> <br /> So, find the important numbers, then find out how they categorize.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-21T14:36:22-07:00","id":1534532,"title":"","content":"no, i meant what sort of spheres would they have?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27683-bernese","name":"Bernese","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-21T16:38:31-07:00","id":1534534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bernese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534473-other-cultures-sphere-systems?p=1534532#post1534532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">no, i meant what sort of spheres would they have?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd need to know their categories. Example: In the Medieval West fire, water, earth, and air were the elements. At the same time in China, water, fire, earth, metal, and wood, were the elements. In the modern West Mind and Spirit are separate categories. In many cultures they aren't.<br /> <br /> I would need to know a culture's categories to know their spheres.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-21T17:26:44-07:00","id":1534535,"title":"","content":"yeah, i want to know their categories<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27683-bernese","name":"Bernese","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-22T00:13:16-07:00","id":1534547,"title":"","content":"Well research the culture in question. That's the way to learn their categories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-22T05:10:05-07:00","id":1534550,"title":"","content":"The difficulty (or at least the tediousness) of doing this is, I suspect, a major reason why it hasn't been done already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-22T06:24:19-07:00","id":1534554,"title":"","content":"Also, one of the great pitfalls of Mage is blurring the line between the spheres as a a game mechanic and the spheres as an in universe system. The mechanics are a gaming abstraction. They don't say anything about the metaphysics of Mage or the characters in game unless you want them to. Every character can be played using the mechanical sphere system, even those which would, in universe, never consider describing their practices using the Traditions sphere descriptions. <br /> <br /> Of course you can choose to have paradigm and practice affect the game mechanics if you want to, but it isn't mandatory. Let the decision be based on the needs of your game and players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-23T07:11:19-07:00","id":1534589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534473-other-cultures-sphere-systems?p=1534554#post1534554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, one of the great pitfalls of Mage is blurring the line between the spheres as a a game mechanic and the spheres as an in universe system. The mechanics are a gaming abstraction. They don't say anything about the metaphysics of Mage or the characters in game unless you want them to. Every character can be played using the mechanical sphere system, even those which would, in universe, never consider describing their practices using the Traditions sphere descriptions.<br /> <br /> Of course you can choose to have paradigm and practice affect the game mechanics if you want to, but it isn't mandatory. Let the decision be based on the needs of your game and players.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's BS talk, which I hear replicated ad nauseum all the time that the idea of &quot;in game&quot; Spheres are brought up. &quot;The game mechanics don't have anything to do with how the in game metaphysics works&quot;...<br /> <br /> Err, sorry, but that's BS. It most definitely do, no matter how much the writers and the players would like that to not be true.<br /> <br /> And it most definitely does defines the metaphysics because you just simply cannot be JUST an &quot;Alchemist&quot; without knowing at least Prime and Matter. But then, this means you'll also know how to make &quot;lightsabers&quot; with Prime 2, even if all that you ever wanted was to concoct a few healing potions.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry, but I have heard this line about how the two (mechanics and in game setting) are oh, so disconnected from each other, I heard that bs non stop for years, but unfortunately this is blatantly false in a huge number of ways.<br /> <br /> In truth, you CANNOT be a &quot;Necromancer&quot; without Spirit, Life, Matter, Prime.<br /> <br /> But that will mean that you'll NEVER be <b>only</b> a Necromancer, since you won't just deal with spooky ghosts, you can also cosplay a shaman and speak with the rocks and the threes, even if all you ever wanted to do was to just be a grave robber.<br /> <br /> Even if all you wanted to do was to make skeletons dance, you'll also have the powah to transmutate lead into gold, because the &quot;soooo abstract&quot; sphere of Matter that you'll use, will enable you to do both.<br /> <br /> So no, that is blatantly FALSE. But I don't know why, people over the years have recited this mantra &quot;mechanics are just an abstraction&quot; for so long, maybe to convince themselves? Maybe to convince themselves that something subpar is actually better than it is?<br /> <br /> I mean I get it, Mage is my favorite thing in the world after my wife and kids, but just like I don't think my kids are perfect and I'm perfect fine to realize their flaws, neither do I need to put Mage on a pedestal and believe that it can do no wrong.<br /> <br /> MtA is not the Holy Graal sent by God that can do no wrong. It certainly can, and the game mechanics for Spheres is certainly one of these cases. Despite the infinite rambles from the writers, and I get it why they would want it to be true and perhaps why they keep repeating it infinitely to the point that I believe they start to believe their own lie, the game mechanics actually severely limits what can be done in universe, and thus it is NOT just a &quot;mere abstraction&quot;. Sorry, but it isn't.<br /> <br /> Sorry for the rant and for the harshness of my answer, but this seriously annoys me to no end.\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-23T08:26:52-07:00","id":1534594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534473-other-cultures-sphere-systems?p=1534589#post1534589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> In truth, you CANNOT be a &quot;Necromancer&quot; without Spirit, Life, Matter, Prime.<br /> <br /> But that will mean that you'll NEVER be <b>only</b> a Necromancer, since you won't just deal with spooky ghosts, you can also cosplay a shaman and speak with the rocks and the threes, even if all you ever wanted to do was to just be a grave robber.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on your paradigm. Paradigm lets you limit what you can do in the narrative. For example you can have a paradigm that limits your spirit use only to the dead.<br /> <br /> If you prefer more mechanical limitations use minor spheres","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 04-23-2024, 11:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-23T09:01:05-07:00","id":1534597,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534473-other-cultures-sphere-systems?p=1534589#post1534589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's BS talk, which I hear replicated ad nauseum all the time that the idea of &quot;in game&quot; Spheres are brought up. &quot;The game mechanics don't have anything to do with how the in game metaphysics works&quot;...<br /> <br /> Err, sorry, but that's BS. It most definitely do, no matter how much the writers and the players would like that to not be true.<br /> <br /> ...Snip..<br /> <br /> So no, that is blatantly FALSE. But I don't know why, people over the years have recited this mantra &quot;mechanics are just an abstraction&quot; for so long, maybe to convince themselves? Maybe to convince themselves that something subpar is actually better than it is?</div> </div> </div> </div>You've presented a very good argument for how the Sphere Mechanics have some major flaws. I agree that the sphere system doesn't do a good job at handling necromancy, and plenty of builds will end up having more powers than they actually use. But that just means that the game system has places it is bad at simulating the game world. It doesn't mean the sphere mechanics are the actual metaphysics of Mage<br /> <br /> It's the same kind of of oversight as someone with a high academics being good at subjects they've never studied. That implies that someone who does an exhaustive study of Wordsworth's poems will somehow pick up knowledge about continental drift, Aztec sacrificial practices, and the sex life of the long extinct Burmese Warbling Finch. We don't treat that as the metaphysics of the game, but as an artifact of the game system we are willing to put up with.<br /> <br /> It reminds me of an old issue in Rifts. Apparently some players were treating the damage rules as actual descriptions of how the world worked. Rifts had a concept called megadamage that I won't go deeply into but meant that, on paper, people could shoot themselves in the head without taking any damage. And some players were doing just that to psych opponents out or make intimidation rolls or something. It worked according to the rules but it didn't match the game world that the rules were supposed to describe. And when asked, the writers said exactly that. The rules may say shooting yourself in the head does no damage, but the shared narrative of the gaming table says that it does.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-23T18:35:30-07:00","id":1534614,"title":"","content":"I mean yes, the Spheres were very obviously intended as mere abstractions. And the game works better overrall when players and Storytellers treat it that way.<br /> <br /> But it's untrue to say the Spheres have no significance in-universe. They very much do, if for no reason than because a sufficient number of Mages have been using the Spheres as a theoretical framework for centuries. The Umbra reflects human belief, and how they conceptualize the world. In the Umbra, the planets in our solar system are tied directly to the Spheres. Pluto's spiritual counterpart IS ALSO the Shard Realm of Entropy. Mars's spiritual counterpart IS ALSO the Shard Realm of Forces.<br /> <br /> Should it be that way? Probably not, since it's very gamey. But Mage is all about how peoples' shared narratives alter how Reality functions. Even if most Mage factions prefer to order their world in their own esoteric ways, that they use the Spheres as an inter-faction framework for discussing Magick means those concepts have a weight all their own. To the point even the Technocracy grudgingly uses the same Spheres (barring Technocratic variants, like Primal Utility or Dimensional Science, of course).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-24T00:52:02-07:00","id":1534624,"title":"","content":"To be fair, the reason why the Technocratic variants exist is because using the Spheres as written for the Technocracy doesn't <i>quite</i> work. <i>Almost; </i>but not quite. Thus, you get Dimensional Science's easily penetrated Gauntlet in a place where the Gauntlet would normally be at its thickest (and in the Revised Convention Book, a restriction in focus when dealing with spirits that still lets you attack them, capture them, and drive them away, but has nothing for more benign interactions with them) and Primal Utility's removal of \u201cglowy Effects\u201d (for lack of a better name) in exchange for having an easier time making Wonders and, when first published, the unique capability to tap into Primal Ventures. Even now, Technocrats have a unique capability to make Devices without having to invest personal Quintessence or Willpower into the effort, something that (like Dimensional Science's ability to penetrate the Gauntlet where it really shouldn't be able to) is restricted to specialized Technocratic infrastructure. <br /> <br /> There's precedent for tweaking the Spheres to produce variants that don't quite work the same as the default write-ups, normally in the form of adding capabilities or making existing capabilities easier to access, but always in exchange for removing other capabilities or making other capabilities harder to access. A shift in capabilities rather than an expansion of capabilities. <br /> <br /> And I personally find it ironic that the only examples we have of this belong to the Technocracy. Why <i>can't</i> we facilitate the use of Necromancy by saying that, e.g., the Euthanatoi have developed a variant of Entropy that makes much more of the things we associate with Necromancy available with just that Sphere variant? I once went through a thought experiment where I considered each of the Traditions with the idea that they might have some unique insights into one or two of the Spheres that let them do things with it that the strict write-ups of those Spheres don't permit. It seemed like a very Traditions-like thing to do. <br /> <br /> With that said, my current view on the subject is to lean into Minor Spheres, like what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28439\" data-vbnamecard=\"28439\">quelsec</a> briefly suggested earlier. The one catch is that the closest thing we have to an official endorsement of this idea is the Revised era's <b>Storyteller's Handbook</b>; and that was explicitly a book about hacking the rules and setting. There's a wonderful STV product (Book of Fragments) that presents a robust system for Minor Spheres which I heartily endorse; but it <i>is</i> a STV product, and not something officially endorsed. <br /> <br /> Sphere Variants and Minor Spheres have the advantage that you can devise one of them at a time, in a vacuum; and even then, it requires significant effort. What <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27683-bernese\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27683\" data-vbnamecard=\"27683\">Bernese</a> asked for here is a <i>whole different organizing principle</i> for the Spheres. That's a <i>much</i> bigger ask. Frankly, the strongest argument I've seen for sticking to the Nine Spheres as written is that the work in writing them up has already been done. From a strictly practical viewpoint: for all their faults, they're something that we already <i>have</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-24T06:55:23-07:00","id":1534630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534473-other-cultures-sphere-systems?p=1534614#post1534614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean yes, the Spheres were very obviously intended as mere abstractions. And the game works better overrall when players and Storytellers treat it that way.<br /> <br /> But it's untrue to say the Spheres have no significance in-universe. They very much do, if for no reason than because a sufficient number of Mages have been using the Spheres as a theoretical framework for centuries. The Umbra reflects human belief, and how they conceptualize the world. In the Umbra, the planets in our solar system are tied directly to the Spheres. Pluto's spiritual counterpart IS ALSO the Shard Realm of Entropy. Mars's spiritual counterpart IS ALSO the Shard Realm of Forces.<br /> <br /> Should it be that way? Probably not, since it's very gamey. But Mage is all about how peoples' shared narratives alter how Reality functions. Even if most Mage factions prefer to order their world in their own esoteric ways, that they use the Spheres as an inter-faction framework for discussing Magick means those concepts have a weight all their own. To the point even the Technocracy grudgingly uses the same Spheres (barring Technocratic variants, like Primal Utility or Dimensional Science, of course).</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, which is why my original post was to distinguish the game mechanics spheres, which are just a gaming abstraction, from the in-universe spheres which, for better or worse, have a presence in things like Certamen and the Shade and Shard* Realms. As you say, though, the existence of the realms doesn't have to mean anything more than that the concept of spheres has built up a metaphysical weight from use. And the mechanics of the Sphere rules don't have to mean anything at all.<br /> <br /> *I originally misspelled this as Shart Realms, which is a typo that needs to be preserved for posterity. Also, &quot;shart&quot; is now in the oxford dictionary, which I did not know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-24T10:02:53-07:00","id":1534650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534473-other-cultures-sphere-systems?p=1534597#post1534597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You've presented a very good argument for how the Sphere Mechanics have some major flaws. I agree that the sphere system doesn't do a good job at handling necromancy, and plenty of builds will end up having more powers than they actually use. But that just means that the game system has places it is bad at simulating the game world. It doesn't mean the sphere mechanics are the actual metaphysics of Mage<br /> <br /> It's the same kind of of oversight as someone with a high academics being good at subjects they've never studied. That implies that someone who does an exhaustive study of Wordsworth's poems will somehow pick up knowledge about continental drift, Aztec sacrificial practices, and the sex life of the long extinct Burmese Warbling Finch. We don't treat that as the metaphysics of the game, but as an artifact of the game system we are willing to put up with.<br /> <br /> It reminds me of an old issue in Rifts. Apparently some players were treating the damage rules as actual descriptions of how the world worked. Rifts had a concept called megadamage that I won't go deeply into but meant that, on paper, people could shoot themselves in the head without taking any damage. And some players were doing just that to psych opponents out or make intimidation rolls or something. It worked according to the rules but it didn't match the game world that the rules were supposed to describe. And when asked, the writers said exactly that. The rules may say shooting yourself in the head does no damage, but the shared narrative of the gaming table says that it does.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. I fully agree. The game mechanics are abstractions, but when they blatantly disregard the world they are supposed to represent, there's a problem.<br /> <br /> I've designed group-specific &quot;Spheres&quot; because of that for my games, but indeed it's a bit of extra work, particularly for new players that already think that Mage is a weird nerdy game. Imagine adding another 30+ Spheres group taylored to it.<br /> <br /> I do think that the idea of &quot;hacked spheres&quot; should be made official, like those from Book of Fragments. A simple supplement would fix this problem. The examples of Alchemy and Necromancy are perhaps the most visible ones, since those are iconic ideas of &quot;magic weavers&quot;, but would be poorly designed using the conventional 9 spheres. For Necromancy for example, you'd need some Spirit, some Matter, some Life, some Entropy, some Prime - at the very least. Someone may just say &quot;oh, Paradigm&quot;. Errr... No. Sorry but now. The only thing Paradigm could do is cripple the Mage with such a belief, not allowing him the full usage of his capabilities. Realistically, if my Paradigm regarding the Life Sphere is all about the end of it, then I theoretically would NOT be learning about non death related life... So, I would not be learning about Metamorphosis, so at the very least it should be cheaper.<br /> <br /> But even that is a poor excuse. Because there are Paradigms that DON'T deal with Necromancy at the expense of everything else. You CANNOT for instance play an Hermetic that is specialized in Necromancy - AKA someone that only cares about studying Necromancy. Because, to study Necromancy you'll need to study about the &quot;meta-magic&quot; of Prime, you'll need to study about the web-flows of Life and so on, and you'll need to take classes on &quot;summoning imps 101&quot; even thou the only thing the guy cares about is to see ghosts. And that's because he's Paradigm embraces Necromancy but do NOT exclude the rest","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-25T12:32:25-07:00","id":1534715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534473-other-cultures-sphere-systems?p=1534650#post1534650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But even that is a poor excuse. Because there are Paradigms that DON'T deal with Necromancy at the expense of everything else. You CANNOT for instance play an Hermetic that is specialized in Necromancy - AKA someone that only cares about studying Necromancy. Because, to study Necromancy you'll need to study about the &quot;meta-magic&quot; of Prime, you'll need to study about the web-flows of Life and so on, and you'll need to take classes on &quot;summoning imps 101&quot; even thou the only thing the guy cares about is to see ghosts. And that's because he's Paradigm embraces Necromancy but do NOT exclude the rest</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd submit that all this talk of a mage who &quot;just wants to learn necromancy and nothing else&quot; is (consciously or not) trying to shove Mage into a standard fantasy box, and it's just not that kind of game. Mages don't approach magick in those terms in M:TA, because *that's not how magick works.*<br /> <br /> Paradigms can (and should) limit how you manifest effects, absolutely. That's why there's a benefit of casting aside tools as your Arete increases. But a lot of the vitriol here seems to be setting up a strawman that Mage never claimed would stand in the setting, then tearing it down angrily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-25T14:02:13-07:00","id":1534733,"title":"","content":"True enough. A case could be made that if you want to play someone who deals in <i>just </i>Necromancy or <i>just </i>Alchemy, you don't actually want a Mage; you want a Sorcerer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-25T14:10:38-07:00","id":1534734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534473-other-cultures-sphere-systems?p=1534733#post1534733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True enough. A case could be made that if you want to play someone who deals in <i>just </i>Necromancy or <i>just </i>Alchemy, you don't actually want a Mage; you want a Sorcerer.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Utterly this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-25T15:30:57-07:00","id":1534739,"title":"","content":"Agree on the linear magic approach for highly specific practice. I'm a bit surprised Foundations and Pillars didn't get a mention yet. They are highly informed by the paradigm of the Fellowships (and thereby limited), while retaining a degree of flexibility that puts the k in Magick. I have to admit though that I'm not sure they fit for what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27683-bernese\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27683\" data-vbnamecard=\"27683\">Bernese</a> is looking for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-26T01:55:43-07:00","id":1534754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534473-other-cultures-sphere-systems?p=1534715#post1534715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd submit that all this talk of a mage who &quot;just wants to learn necromancy and nothing else&quot; is (consciously or not) trying to shove Mage into a standard fantasy box, and it's just not that kind of game. Mages don't approach magick in those terms in M:TA, because *that's not how magick works.*<br /> <br /> Paradigms can (and should) limit how you manifest effects, absolutely. That's why there's a benefit of casting aside tools as your Arete increases. But a lot of the vitriol here seems to be setting up a strawman that Mage never claimed would stand in the setting, then tearing it down angrily.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. While it's very possible for a Mage to pursue, for example, Necromancy as a specialty, this doesn't mean they couldn't or wouldn't learn magical tricks outside that narrow box. Partly because pre-modern magical practitioners kept ALL their knowledge close to their chest, so any given Mage took whatever knowledge they could get. And partly because their Focus isn't a narrow band of thematically related powers (even Sorcerer Paths aren't always that, as evidenced by the flexible nature of Hellfire), but a holistic approach to viewing and interacting with the world around them.<br /> <br /> To be a Mage is to adhere to a lifestyle that carries with it both a broad understanding of their Reality, and a certain measure of <i>responsibility</i>. Dreamspeakers and Verbana are often most associated with this, as they have a duty to both their communities/families and to the spirits/old gods. Not to mention the practical applications of their Magick, for themselves, which leads them to learn a broad swathe of Rotes.<br /> <br /> For Necromancy, you might look at the Euthanatos Mage. They may specialize in dealing with the dead, whether their spirits or their corporeal remains. But they're also interested heavily in Fate. Learning how to read and manipulate Fate as it pertains to mortality, by necessity of their world view, also means acquiring the tools and framework for reading and manipulating Fate in other ways. These are not necessarily extricable, because the mystics and culture broadly that developed these tools did not neatly divide one application from another, nor consider it advantageous to do so. If your forebears went to the trouble learning how to reanimate a corpse via mastery of the principles of life (or Life), they wouldn't balk at using those same principles to heal the wounds and illnesses of themselves and others. Nor at using them to empower their bodies.<br /> <br /> Euthanatoi, as a Tradition, is also very interested in employing their Magick for the purposes of giving the Good Death. Whether that's helping a sick person find rest, or eliminating a wicked person so they can no longer do harm. There are many ways in which learning the fundamentals of their Focus, for use in interacting with the dead, could also be employed to MAKE people dead. Since giving the Good Death is considered a utility/responsibility unto itself, no Euthanatos would balk at learning any tool they can to accomplish it. (Indeed, the Chakravanti consider over-reliance on death Magick to be dangerous, as it can lead to Jhor. So being &quot;more balanced&quot; is advantageous in itself).<br /> <br /> The strength of being a Mage is in not just having a hammer, and seeing everything as a nail.<br /> <br /> (On the flipside, if a Mage or their Player WANTS to focus their knowledge of a given Sphere only on one application, for thematic reasons, there's nothing stopping them from doing so. It just becomes an in-universe and out-of-universe choice. If the Necromancer wanted to gain dots in Time solely to see into the past or future, or to age someone to dust, that's fine. It just shouldn't be seen as a failure of the Sphere system if you think all your powers should be in one progression track. If that's what you want, create a few Minor Spheres related to Necromancy.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 04-26-2024, 05:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-26T03:35:54-07:00","id":1534757,"title":"","content":"Again though, keep in mind that Minor Spheres aren't official, much as I would like them to be. <br /> <br /> Then again, Mage in general is more accepting of non-official than most gamelines; M20 in particular features \u201cit's your game; do as you will\u201d from the author.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-28T11:35:09-07:00","id":1534854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534473-other-cultures-sphere-systems?p=1534733#post1534733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True enough. A case could be made that if you want to play someone who deals in <i>just </i>Necromancy or <i>just </i>Alchemy, you don't actually want a Mage; you want a Sorcerer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah. Maybe I'm intrigued about the concepts of Alchemy AND dimensional space. <br /> <br /> Let me remind you that the &quot;study&quot; of Alchemy is a REAL world &quot;mystical study&quot;. There is, there really are (even to this day) people who study the magical traditions of Alchemy. Heck, Isaac Newton was an Alchemist.<br /> <br /> It is PERFECTLY FITTING to study Alchemy while you also try to reach the Astral Plane to meet the &quot;Hermetic Masters&quot;. In fact, real world Hermetic cults do this to this day.<br /> <br /> My point is that someone interested in Alchemy shouldn't need to learn about &quot;Entropy&quot; just so he can understand the mystical-philosophical meanings of the metaphysics of transmutation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-28T11:43:06-07:00","id":1534855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534473-other-cultures-sphere-systems?p=1534734#post1534734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This. Utterly this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wrong. You do NOT want a Sorceror. Maybe you just simply want to play a Psychopomp Witch Doctor who is, you know, a REAL WORLD religious/magical practice, upon which &quot;Necromancy&quot; is only of the tools under his utility belt, but he can also delve into &quot;normal&quot; Mind and Correspondence too. A Witch Doctor practitioner of Umbanda for instance, a religion to which I actually know of because my wife is a practitioner. I can tell you, they believe they deal in some form of &quot;Necromancy Magic&quot; by speaking with the death, but also &quot;Time&quot; (predictions of the future and past&quot;), Correspondence (clairvoyance) and Entropy (curses and blessings). Also Mind too and a few others.<br /> <br /> They DON'T deal with spirits of rocks and threes, they can heal or &quot;detect Life&quot;, but don't do Wicca stuff to shapeshift into cats.<br /> <br /> It just doesn't fit with the 9 Spheres","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-28T19:30:23-07:00","id":1534873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534473-other-cultures-sphere-systems?p=1534855#post1534855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It just doesn't fit with the 9 Spheres</div> </div> </div> </div>That was my point. Mage doesn't work that way. Sorcerer works much closer to that way.<br /> <br /> Homebrewing in lesser/minor spheres is fine for your table, if that's the way you feel to best resolve the situation. But I don't understand why you are angrily arguing that Mage, as published, doesn't do a thing it never claimed to do. Metaphisics in the world of Mage work the way the rules describe. While they may have some basis in or inspiration from real world practices, they are presented to adhere to the game's base assumptions.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-28T20:14:12-07:00","id":1534876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534473-other-cultures-sphere-systems?p=1534873#post1534873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was my point. Mage doesn't work that way. Sorcerer works much closer to that way.<br /> <br /> Homebrewing in lesser/minor spheres is fine for your table, if that's the way you feel to best resolve the situation. But I don't understand why you are angrily arguing that Mage, as published, doesn't do a thing it never claimed to do. Metaphisics in the world of Mage work the way the rules describe. While they may have some basis in or inspiration from real world practices, they are presented to adhere to the game's base assumptions.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>They do NOT adhere to the game's assumptions thou. They only adhere to the Hermetic/Gnostic-Animistic metaphysics that is implicit throughout the entirety of the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> You need no greater proof of that than the 2 original &quot;new Spheres&quot; that are exclusive to the Technocracy from Rev and M20. The only reason as to why &quot;Dimensional Science&quot; exists at all is because Spirit is a poor fit for a game mechanics to the Union; and no, they are NOT the same Sphere with different names, regardless of the similarities.<br /> <br /> I think you're the one that is not seeing how the Spheres don't actually reflect the Metaphysics of Mage - heck, the very game makes the claim that they are simple abstractions used for game mechanics purposes only. The 9 Spheres (11 actually, if you count the 2 Technocratic variations) are NOT the codex of the laws of the Cosmos.<br /> <br /> My point is that, as game mechanics abstractions, they do a somewhat good job on a simplistic level, but are a poor fit for anything deeper than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-28T20:33:32-07:00","id":1534877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534473-other-cultures-sphere-systems?p=1534739#post1534739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agree on the linear magic approach for highly specific practice. I'm a bit surprised Foundations and Pillars didn't get a mention yet. They are highly informed by the paradigm of the Fellowships (and thereby limited), while retaining a degree of flexibility that puts the k in Magick. I have to admit though that I'm not sure they fit for what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27683-bernese\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27683\" data-vbnamecard=\"27683\">Bernese</a> is looking for.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't touched upon Foundations and Pillars because I just simply thought those would be the obvious answer, while at the same time not exactly what OP wanted. But yes, I do think they have something going in the right direction. However, &quot;customized Spheres&quot; are still my choice. And I now that's not canon, obviously, everybody knows that. So that's my rant, I think it should be canon, I think it should at least be a canon optional rule. For instance, my Dreamspeakers and Ecstatics have only 3 Spheres, Body, Mind and Sprit, related to the &quot;Illusion of Matter&quot; (Body), the world of the senses (Mind) and the &quot;superior&quot; or &quot;real&quot; world of the &quot;forms&quot; (Spirit - something akin to Plato's allegory of the cave).<br /> <br /> That's a game mechanics abstraction that simply shows that, for an Ecstatic, they don't differentiate (in esoteric metaphysics) between a living beings, a rock or a lightning, since it's all just an illusion of &quot;matter&quot;, hence why they learn how to &quot;manipulate the material dream&quot; all at once; imagining a bit of Matrix, &quot;there is no spoon&quot;. There is no spoon. There is no rock and no cat, there is just an illusion of a rock or a cat, when in reality, the &quot;real reality&quot; is just 'Spirit', is just Ephemera.<br /> <br /> Roughly speaking, in terms of game mechanics, the Sphere of &quot;Body&quot; deals with the same as the classic Life, Matter, Forces, while &quot;Mind&quot; deals with Correspondence, Time, Entropy (no, the classic &quot;Mind&quot; doesn't enter here, the Dreamspeakers and Ecstatics Sphere of &quot;Mind&quot; deals with the sensorial illusions around us, therefore the &quot;illusions&quot; of time, space and &quot;action/reaction&quot;, which you could call &quot;Entropy&quot;). And then, &quot;Spirit&quot; deals with the &quot;real reality&quot;, so it encompasses the classic Spheres of Mind, Spirit and Prime.<br /> <br /> And yes, in this Paradigm, there's no real difference between &quot;Mind&quot; and &quot;Spirit&quot;, they see it as one and the same thing, and that separation is somewhat nonsensical.<br /> <br /> Thus, there you go, 3 Spheres, Body, Mind, Spirit, just game mechanics abstractions that better reflect such a worldview. Thus, an Ecstatic learning &quot;Spirit&quot; 1, 2 or 3 will be studying and learning how to talk with the dead, how to talk with the spirits of the threes and how to reach the minds of the living because TO HIM, THOSE ARE ALL ONE AND THE SAME. Reading minds with this version of Spirit 3 requires the same kind of mystical knowledge/insight as summoning ephemeral beings of the spirit world.<br /> <br /> That's just one example to illustrate my point. It's not about the metaphysics of the game, but rather about having best abstractions as game mechanics that can better reflect those metaphysics","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-28T20:40:02-07:00","id":1534878,"title":"","content":"Going with just three Spheres that cover everything that the standard nine Spheres cover is problematic from a game rules perspective, and leads to the question of why madness wouldn't gravitate to the Traditions that utilize the fewest Spheres.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-28T21:27:40-07:00","id":1534881,"title":"","content":"I think you're all too fixated on my 2 simple examples, but those were just the first 2 that came in my mind. And you're too focused on the idea that &quot;Necromancy&quot; or &quot;Alchemy&quot; are almost just an RPG trope or even a simple &quot;style&quot; - which isn't exactly true, after all there are many Thanatoic religions throughout the world that have their worldview based on what we could describe as &quot;Necromancy&quot; for simplistic reasons, and &quot;Alchemy&quot; is not merely trying to turn lead into gold, but a rather metaphysical worldview about the changes in the cosmos. So no, they aren't exactly &quot;just sorcery material&quot;, but ok, I understand where you're coming from.<br /> <br /> The 2 unique Spheres of the Technocracy are other examples however.<br /> <br /> I can also come up with other easily understandable examples, and examples that BREAK THE 9 SPHERES WHILE BEING COMPLETELY CANON.<br /> <br /> 2 examples: Space/Time &quot;Sphere&quot; and &quot;Biochemistry Sphere&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'll explain: imagine an &quot;Enlightened Scientist&quot; that sees Space and Time as fundamentally the same. So, for this Techie boy (or maybe, Techie-mancer), there is no &quot;Correspondence&quot; or &quot;Time&quot; Spheres, but rather he studies the &quot;Sphere of Space/Time&quot;.<br /> <br /> And how could that keep up with canon?<br /> <br /> Simple. The player tells the ST that &quot;my guy sees Space and Time as the same thing&quot;.<br /> <br /> And, to that, the ST simply answers &quot;Very well. Therefore, you can NOT buy Correspondence or Time individually, you HAVE TO buy a level on BOTH any time you wish to increase your knowledge about Space/Time&quot;.<br /> <br /> But wait, the player himself can do it, even if the ST himself dislikes the idea; the player can simply state &quot;Because my Enlightened Scientist believes that Space and Time are one and the same, I'll only ever buy a level on either Correspondence or Time it I simultaneously also buy the same level on the other Sphere&quot;.<br /> <br /> BAM. You just demolished the idea that the cosmos has a metaphysics that is divided into 9 Spheres; essentially, you reduced the number of Spheres to 8, while having one of them that is harder to grasp/learn (because the &quot;hacked&quot; Sphere of &quot;Space/Time&quot; costs double the XP - but XP is also just another game mechanics abstraction).<br /> <br /> The same kind of hack could be applied to an Enlightened Scientist that believes that &quot;Matter&quot; and &quot;Life&quot; are fundamentally the same - chemical reactions with different degrees of complexity. Thus, the player could also &quot;hack the system&quot; in order to create a &quot;phantom Sphere&quot; of &quot;Biochemistry&quot;.<br /> <br /> And that's the thing, Spheres are just game mechanics abstractions, they are NOT the &quot;laws of the cosmos&quot;.<br /> <br /> The other example we could &quot;hack&quot; in the exactly same way without moving even a millimeter (or an inch for my American friends) from official canon, would be to create an amalgamation Sphere of Mind+Spirit for my Mystical Mage that sees no distinctions between mind and spirits... For my Mage, a person's Mind IS HIS SOUL, and Spirits are essentially &quot;ephemeral Minds&quot;. My previous example on the 3 Spheres for Ecstatics and Dreamspeakers illustrate this quite well - and hell, the idea of them having only the 3 Spheres of Body, Mind and Sprit can also be &quot;hacked&quot; in much the same way.<br /> <br /> So, we actually CAN use the abstractions of the game mechanics in order to change the number of Spheres the game has, but this is limited to only grouping the existing ones to form new ones. Space/Time can be created by purchasing Time+Correspondence on a single package, Biochemistry by buying Life+Matter, and the single &quot;Mind=Spirit&quot; Sphere by buying those together. Since it's all just abstractions, that's not just feasible, but it also strictly follows the holy canon laws to the letter.<br /> <br /> I'm simply stating that this same idea should be applied in a much broader range, for example, instead of creating new Spheres by merging the existing ones, to allow this process to be done by splitting them or taking few pieces of several different ones into one single amalgamation; Necromancy, for instance, could be the amalgamation of small pieces from Spirit, Entropy, Prime, Matter, Life (and perhaps others).<br /> <br /> That's all that I'm suggesting, an expansion on the scope and the capabilities described by the game mechanics abstractions that the official Spheres represent.<br /> <br /> Another example that I really like, is the &quot;Minor Sphere&quot; of &quot;Memetics&quot;. Initially called &quot;Dogma&quot; (Sorcerors Crusade), then called &quot;Propaganda&quot;, and now called &quot;Memetics&quot;. This is the study of how ideas are spread throughout societies, and thus to use that knowledge to influence it. That's the main &quot;secret weapon&quot; of the Technocracy on my games, and their mastery of this Science is how they managed to get on top of the Ascension War.<br /> <br /> Mind would be a poor fit for it, since you can't really affect millions of individuals all at once (since you would need millions of successes per RAW). The only more or less adaptable kind of effects for this would require, well, Entropy 5!<br /> <br /> Instead, I use the Sphere of &quot;Memetics&quot;. Bam, problem solved. An entire Sphere dedicated solely for the brainwashing of entire societies through the &quot;magikal&quot; use of mass propaganda. It also makes the Technocracy so much more scary and pervasive in the game. And you won't have master propagandists in the Union who also happen to be &quot;mister Lucky Agent&quot; because of the silly requirement of also needing to have everything else that comes with Entropy 5 just as a prerequisite to become a &quot;master propagandist&quot; in the first place.<br /> <br /> That's the kind of mechanics that I want, and I see no reason as to why those can't or shouldn't be implemented, particularly, as I said, you can already merge Spheres together on a practical manner if you wish so <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-28T21:51:57-07:00","id":1534883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534473-other-cultures-sphere-systems?p=1534878#post1534878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going with just three Spheres that cover everything that the standard nine Spheres cover is problematic from a game rules perspective, and leads to the question of why madness wouldn't gravitate to the Traditions that utilize the fewest Spheres.</div> </div> </div> </div>3 Spheres, each costing 3 times more than the &quot;classic&quot; 9 Spheres.<br /> <br /> If I decide that I'll only ever buy Life, Matter and Forces all at once in &quot;the same package&quot;, only raising a level in any of those if I also raise a level in the other 2 at the same time, and calling it the &quot;Body (or Material) Sphere&quot;, is essentially the same as the game just outright telling me &quot;here's the Body Sphere that costs 3 times more XP and allows you to make any change whatsoever on any type of patterns that are strictly from the material plane&quot;. It's essentially the same thing.<br /> <br /> The same goes if I decide to buy Correspondence, Time and Entropy on a single package while claiming it to be the &quot;Mind Sphere&quot;, or if I decide to buy Prime, Spirit and Mind in a single package and unofficially call it the &quot;Spirit Sphere&quot;. It makes no practical difference.<br /> <br /> What's the difference between buying Life+Matter+Forces on a single package and unofficially call it &quot;Body Sphere&quot; from if the game actually said &quot;create your own custom tailored Spheres using these X rules; here's the example of the custom Body Sphere...&quot;<br /> <br /> As for non-game-mechanics questions, you are again conflatating the abstractions that game mechanics should represent to Cosmological truths. And that's EXACTLY why I have a problem with the classic 9 Spheres, precisely because, even if we wrote on every single page of the book that &quot;game mechanics are abstractions intended to represent the world in a manner that makes sense for a game rather than being the actual metaphysics of the world&quot;, even if that was there, players and STs would still conflate the game mechanics with the metaphysics of the setting.<br /> <br /> So no, having &quot;fewer Spheres&quot; doesn't mean being more prone to becoming a Marauder - not necessarily at least, thou it could happen by mere coincidence; for example, those Dreamspeakers and Ecstatics that believe that everything we see and experience in our existences are just a bunch of illusions, and that we are actually just a bunch of incorporeal minds floating in the ether while dreaming that we exist in a world of matter, a very Kantian or Gnostic idea of &quot;immaterialism&quot;, well... I'd say that such a Paradigm is probably more prone towards a mental breakdown and psychotic episode of disconnectiom from reality than an Enlightened Scientist that believes that everything that is exists due to chains of causes and effects in a mechanicist universe that operates under rational and understandable rules is... But that's because the Paradigm of those guys is already a bit nuts, not because of the game mechanic used to better describe it.<br /> <br /> As an example, we could have the Technocracy operate under a set of just 7 Spheres, because we could eliminate Life, Matter, Correspondence and Time and replace those with Biochemistry and Space/Time, and that wouldn't make the Union any more prone to losing their grip over reality any more than they already are.<br /> <br /> As for the part of &quot;harder on a game rules perspective&quot;, I don't disagree. It is somewhat harder for me to keep track over Techies using Space/Time, Biochemistry and Memetics Spheres and having each of the Traditions basically having their single set of personal Spheres, at least before getting used to them, which is why that I fully understand why using the &quot;classic&quot; canon 9 Spheres for simplicity sake, but I also think that those alternatives could easily be provided over by optional rules. &quot;If you want to use your Memetic Wizards, use *these* optional rules to create your custom tailored Sphere of Memetics&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-28T23:09:11-07:00","id":1534887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534473-other-cultures-sphere-systems?p=1534877#post1534877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't touched upon Foundations and Pillars because I just simply thought those would be the obvious answer, while at the same time not exactly what OP wanted. But yes, I do think they have something going in the right direction. However, &quot;customized Spheres&quot; are still my choice. And I now that's not canon, obviously, everybody knows that. So that's my rant, I think it should be canon, I think it should at least be a canon optional rule. For instance, my Dreamspeakers and Ecstatics have only 3 Spheres, Body, Mind and Sprit, related to the &quot;Illusion of Matter&quot; (Body), the world of the senses (Mind) and the &quot;superior&quot; or &quot;real&quot; world of the &quot;forms&quot; (Spirit - something akin to Plato's allegory of the cave).<br /> <br /> That's a game mechanics abstraction that simply shows that, for an Ecstatic, they don't differentiate (in esoteric metaphysics) between a living beings, a rock or a lightning, since it's all just an illusion of &quot;matter&quot;, hence why they learn how to &quot;manipulate the material dream&quot; all at once; imagining a bit of Matrix, &quot;there is no spoon&quot;. There is no spoon. There is no rock and no cat, there is just an illusion of a rock or a cat, when in reality, the &quot;real reality&quot; is just 'Spirit', is just Ephemera.<br /> <br /> Roughly speaking, in terms of game mechanics, the Sphere of &quot;Body&quot; deals with the same as the classic Life, Matter, Forces, while &quot;Mind&quot; deals with Correspondence, Time, Entropy (no, the classic &quot;Mind&quot; doesn't enter here, the Dreamspeakers and Ecstatics Sphere of &quot;Mind&quot; deals with the sensorial illusions around us, therefore the &quot;illusions&quot; of time, space and &quot;action/reaction&quot;, which you could call &quot;Entropy&quot;). And then, &quot;Spirit&quot; deals with the &quot;real reality&quot;, so it encompasses the classic Spheres of Mind, Spirit and Prime.<br /> <br /> And yes, in this Paradigm, there's no real difference between &quot;Mind&quot; and &quot;Spirit&quot;, they see it as one and the same thing, and that separation is somewhat nonsensical.<br /> <br /> Thus, there you go, 3 Spheres, Body, Mind, Spirit, just game mechanics abstractions that better reflect such a worldview. Thus, an Ecstatic learning &quot;Spirit&quot; 1, 2 or 3 will be studying and learning how to talk with the dead, how to talk with the spirits of the threes and how to reach the minds of the living because TO HIM, THOSE ARE ALL ONE AND THE SAME. Reading minds with this version of Spirit 3 requires the same kind of mystical knowledge/insight as summoning ephemeral beings of the spirit world.<br /> <br /> That's just one example to illustrate my point. It's not about the metaphysics of the game, but rather about having best abstractions as game mechanics that can better reflect those metaphysics</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you got it wrong here. To cast spells acording to your paradigm you need ABILITIES that reflect that paradigm on the level of spheres you are using. Those abilities also reflect if you can do something, irrevelant to the actual sphere level. So picking a paradigm you can focus on just necromancy simply not having the abilities needed to use it for other things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 04-29-2024, 02:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-29T09:40:53-07:00","id":1534906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534473-other-cultures-sphere-systems?p=1534887#post1534887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you got it wrong here. To cast spells acording to your paradigm you need ABILITIES that reflect that paradigm on the level of spheres you are using. Those abilities also reflect if you can do something, irrevelant to the actual sphere level. So picking a paradigm you can focus on just necromancy simply not having the abilities needed to use it for other things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I understood what you meant. Are you referring to things like knowing how to dance or sing or paint that you use for your effects?<br /> <br /> I'm not sure that's what you meant, so if it isn't please forgive me because I did not understood. If it is what you meant thou, then those would be a part of the foci you use for the effect, while the Spheres reflects more of a sort of &quot;theoretical Thaumatology&quot; that you use for the spell.<br /> <br /> For instance, you might have &quot;dance&quot; as the Focus of your spell; surely you need to know how to dance to use it, obviously.<br /> <br /> But in order to use &quot;Dance&quot; as a Focus to summon a spirit... You need to actually have the &quot;arcane knowledge&quot; required to know how to summon spirits - in which case, it would be the Spirit Sphere.<br /> <br /> The skill to Dance however, is unrelated to your &quot;arcane insight&quot; on the Sphere of Spirit thou. You can perform artistic dancing without summoning spirits; you can also summon spirits by tightening your sphincter really tight and wishing it so very very much if needed be (casting without a Focus). Those two are not actually linked in any way, so I'm not exactly sure of what you mean here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-29T23:52:33-07:00","id":1534931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534473-other-cultures-sphere-systems?p=1534906#post1534906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure I understood what you meant. Are you referring to things like knowing how to dance or sing or paint that you use for your effects?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite. Hear me out here cause it can be a lot.<br /> <br /> 1) the skills are tied to the practice part of paradigm. You can make the skills you dont want in spheres be hidden behind a skill you did not take. As you need a level x skill to use a level x sphere it can be a mechanical solution to the problem. Thats not all though.<br /> <br /> 2) Paradigm as a whole shifts. You ma start as a necromancer but with arete dots your character should change. That includes knowing more about your paradigm but also changes in it and even in the characters nature. So you should not in my opinion play mage thinking you will stay the same and plan his development. It should mutate naturally over the course of play influenced by game events and seekings.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-30T07:08:19-07:00","id":1534943,"title":"","content":"quelsec: that's technically only partially true. Abilities aren't <i>necessarily </i>required to work an Effect, though the Storyteller <i>can</i> call for such a requirement of he thinks it's appropriate to do so. Note that that's partially a question of the Focus involved: some lean heavily on the idea of acquired knowledge and/or practice makes perfect; and in those cases, skills, knowledges, and talents probably should be required. But then you get Foci built around such things as Crazy Wisdom or Faith, where the idea that you study or train yourself is antithetical to the Paradigm or Practice. <br /> <br /> Really, <i>the </i>limitation on what Effects a mage can perform, other than \u201cwhat Spheres do you have\u201d, is \u201cwhat do you think is possible?\u201d If a mage doesn't think he can do something, then he can't do it, even if he has the necessary Spheres to pull it off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-30T20:59:00-07:00","id":1534980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534473-other-cultures-sphere-systems?p=1534931#post1534931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not quite. Hear me out here cause it can be a lot.<br /> <br /> 1) the skills are tied to the practice part of paradigm. You can make the skills you dont want in spheres be hidden behind a skill you did not take. As you need a level x skill to use a level x sphere it can be a mechanical solution to the problem. Thats not all though.<br /> <br /> 2) Paradigm as a whole shifts. You ma start as a necromancer but with arete dots your character should change. That includes knowing more about your paradigm but also changes in it and even in the characters nature. So you should not in my opinion play mage thinking you will stay the same and plan his development. It should mutate naturally over the course of play influenced by game events and seekings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. I'm still not sure I understood perfectly, but as Dataweaver pointed out, Spheres aren't tied to skills. You could have a Catholic templar that believes that all he needs is faith, thus the only thing he ever does is to pray to God for a miracle... And God answers. Or a Psionic just needs to contract his sphincter really tight, and the power of his mind unleash his psionic abilities.<br /> <br /> Paradigm shifts, that much is true, but I find it almost asinine that, say, a Hermetic, who &quot;wasted&quot; his life studying the connections of the Decans with the Zodiac, the 4 humours and the rules of connection of &quot;as above so below&quot; and the wizard's circle represented by the Ouroboros, has a sudden &quot;realization&quot; and &quot;converts&quot; to the shamanism of the Dreamspeakers and toss away all that &quot;silly Zodiac stuff&quot; in favor of animistic ritualism, but everything he learned about his Correspondence 4 related to &quot;sacred geometry&quot;, know is immediately and easily convertible towards &quot;spiritual pathways&quot; in a dime. Or a techie boy that studied &quot;Hyper Chemistry&quot; his entire life to reach matter 5, holding a huge baggage about atoms and chemical reactions, now can just use that while using the &quot;Laws of Similarity&quot; because he converted to a Hermetic.<br /> <br /> Essentially, the way that a Hermetic looks at the Sphere of Life is NOT the same way that a Progenitor does, and that knowledge should NOT be just &quot;the same thing&quot;. Each group has completely and abysmally different paths towards the acquisition of their &quot;arcane&quot; knowledge.<br /> <br /> Again, an Enlightened Scientist that is a fan of Einstein and believes that Space/Time is the same thing, won't develop the Sphere(s) of Space (Corr) and Time in the same way as an Ecstatic that believes that Space/Time are just an illusion created by the dream of the God Bhrama. In fact, he would think that the Ecstatic is just a lunatic!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-01T02:17:32-07:00","id":1534991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534473-other-cultures-sphere-systems?p=1534980#post1534980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm. I'm still not sure I understood perfectly, but as Dataweaver pointed out, Spheres aren't tied to skills. You could have a Catholic templar that believes that all he needs is faith, thus the only thing he ever does is to pray to God for a miracle... And God answers. Or a Psionic just needs to contract his sphincter really tight, and the power of his mind unleash his psionic abilities.<br /> <br /> Paradigm shifts, that much is true, but I find it almost asinine that, say, a Hermetic, who &quot;wasted&quot; his life studying the connections of the Decans with the Zodiac, the 4 humours and the rules of connection of &quot;as above so below&quot; and the wizard's circle represented by the Ouroboros, has a sudden &quot;realization&quot; and &quot;converts&quot; to the shamanism of the Dreamspeakers and toss away all that &quot;silly Zodiac stuff&quot; in favor of animistic ritualism, but everything he learned about his Correspondence 4 related to &quot;sacred geometry&quot;, know is immediately and easily convertible towards &quot;spiritual pathways&quot; in a dime. Or a techie boy that studied &quot;Hyper Chemistry&quot; his entire life to reach matter 5, holding a huge baggage about atoms and chemical reactions, now can just use that while using the &quot;Laws of Similarity&quot; because he converted to a Hermetic.<br /> <br /> Essentially, the way that a Hermetic looks at the Sphere of Life is NOT the same way that a Progenitor does, and that knowledge should NOT be just &quot;the same thing&quot;. Each group has completely and abysmally different paths towards the acquisition of their &quot;arcane&quot; knowledge.<br /> <br /> Again, an Enlightened Scientist that is a fan of Einstein and believes that Space/Time is the same thing, won't develop the Sphere(s) of Space (Corr) and Time in the same way as an Ecstatic that believes that Space/Time are just an illusion created by the dream of the God Bhrama. In fact, he would think that the Ecstatic is just a lunatic!</div> </div> </div> </div>The book says on pages 500-501:<br /> &quot;Step Two \u2013 Ability: Based on your mage\u2019s focus and<br /> Spheres, figure out if you can create the Effect you want<br /> to create\u2026 and if so, how your character will make it<br /> happen in story terms&quot;<br /> For me that ment: do you have the abilities high enought that you need using your practice to get the effect","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-01T05:13:42-07:00","id":1534993,"title":"","content":"And that's a perfectly legitimate house rule. But elsewhere in the book, you'll find advice to the effect of \u201cthe Storyteller can decide that it's appropriate for a particular Practice to require you to have x dots in an appropriate Ability in order to work a particular Effect.\u201d That is, exactly what you described, but as a case by case thing rather than a ubiquitous mandate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-01T06:42:01-07:00","id":1534996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1534473-other-cultures-sphere-systems?p=1534991#post1534991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The book says on pages 500-501:<br /> &quot;Step Two \u2013 Ability: Based on your mage\u2019s focus and<br /> Spheres, figure out if you can create the Effect you want<br /> to create\u2026 and if so, how your character will make it<br /> happen in story terms&quot;<br /> For me that ment: do you have the abilities high enought that you need using your practice to get the effect</div> </div> </div> </div>That section was not describing the abilities that are present in the character sheet (not even optional additional ones).<br /> <br /> It is saying that you need the &quot;ability&quot;, the capability to actually do the effect - based on your focus and Spheres.<br /> <br /> For instance, your techieboy cannot throw &quot;fireball&quot; except if using his Laser Beam XR Gatling Gun. That's his Focus.<br /> <br /> Does he have Forces 3 and Prime 2 and 1 quint to do it? And does he have his Gatling Laser Gun Focus with him? If he does, then he can, if he lacks any of those, he doesn't.<br /> <br /> That's what &quot;ability&quot; means, it is literally the ABILITY TO UNLEASH THE EFFECT.<br /> <br /> It has nothing to do with the list of abilities present in the character sheet, like Conduction, Firearms, Meditation, Athletics and so on.<br /> <br /> This has been so ever since the 1st edition, and remained so in the 2nd ed, Rev (3rd ed) and thus it is also so in M20, which is the one you're quoting. And I guess that their use of the word &quot;Ability&quot; may have caused this unintentional confusion.<br /> <br /> You want to turn into a butterfly? Ok, fair enough.<br /> <br /> Do you have the 'ability' to do so however? Well, that depends. Do you have Life 4? Do you have the appropriate Focus according to your Paradigm?<br /> <br /> If you do meet all of the criteria above, then you do have the 'ability' to cast the spell. If you don't have any of the above, then you don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}